#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Summarize mirrored AVI alongside the pre-existing ABF evidence."""
import csv,collections
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent/'results';Q=P/'avi_mirror'; rows=list(csv.DictReader((Q/'variant_evidence_avi.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t')); regions=list(csv.DictReader((P/'regions.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t')); ids={r['candidate_locus_id'] for r in regions}
assert len(rows)==425 and len(ids)==6

def phred(r):
    a,b=float(r['avi_phred_lower']),float(r['avi_phred_upper'])
    return f'{a:.3f}' if a==b else f'{a:.3f}–{b:.3f}'
def pip(x):return f'{float(x):.3f}' if x else 'not available'
def link(r):return f"[{r['snp']}]({r['atlas_url']})"
lines=['# Brain6 × AlphaGenome: six-region AVI pilot','','**Status:** 425 of 425 prepared candidate–variant rows have an overall AlphaGenome Variant Impact (AVI) score from a pinned third-party re-encoding of Google DeepMind’s static SNV dataset. Subsequently, frontal-cortex reference and alternate predictions were obtained for one variant per region; see the separate [prediction report](../jbrowse_predictions/FRONTAL_CORTEX_REPORT.md).','', 'AVI is a composite prioritization score that includes AlphaGenome regulatory predictions and other inputs. Its PHRED scale expresses a genome-wide rank, not a probability of causality or an estimate of disease risk. A higher score does not identify a tissue, gene, direction of effect or shared causal mechanism. Results concern the union of the previously reported single-signal ABF credible sets, not every regional GWAS variant.','','## Chromosome 5 case study','', 'The chr5:103,447,968–104,447,968 GRCh37 candidate contains 71 selected variants. The highest mirrored AVI score in this selected set belongs to rs2431108 (GRCh38 chr5:104612267:T>C). Its PHRED score is 19.99941; the prior Brain6 conditional ABF PIPs are 0.131 for insomnia and 0.244 for ADHD. Both PIPs depend on the single-causal-variant model; none of these values establishes that the variant is causal. The exploratory trait–trait PP.H4 was 0.991 at p12=10⁻⁵ and 0.917 at p12=10⁻⁶.','', '| Variant | GRCh38 variant | AVI PHRED interval | Insomnia ABF PIP | ADHD ABF PIP | Credible-set membership |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
chr5=[x for x in rows if x['candidate_locus_id']=='placo_insomnia__adhd_chr5_103447968_104447968']
for r in sorted(chr5,key=lambda x:-int(x['avi_raw_e5']))[:10]:
    members=', '.join(t for t in ('insomnia','adhd') if r[t+'_credible_set_member']=='YES')
    lines.append(f"| {link(r)} | {r['atlas_variant']} | {phred(r)} | {pip(r['insomnia_conditional_abf_pip'])} | {pip(r['adhd_conditional_abf_pip'])} | {members} |")
lines += ['', 'Ordering is by the mirror’s exact integer raw AVI score, with no threshold. PIP and AVI are different types of evidence and are not combined into a causal probability. PHRED intervals reflect ties introduced by the published rounded raw score.','', '## All six regions','', '| Candidate region (GRCh37) | Selected variants | Highest AVI in selected set | AVI PHRED interval | PP.H4, p12=10⁻⁵ | PP.H4, p12=10⁻⁶ |','|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for g in regions:
    a=[r for r in rows if r['candidate_locus_id']==g['candidate_locus_id']]; top=max(a,key=lambda r:int(r['avi_raw_e5']));cid=g['candidate_locus_id'].replace('placo_insomnia__adhd_','').replace('_',':',1).replace('_','–')
    lines.append(f"| {cid} | {len(a)} | {link(top)} | {phred(top)} | {float(g['PP_H4_p12_1e-5']):.3f} | {float(g['PP_H4_p12_1e-6']):.3f} |")
lines += ['', 'The chr11, chr14 and lower-coordinate chr5 insomnia units did not pass the original association-posterior gate for an insomnia credible set. Their selected variants come from the ADHD credible sets; reporting an insomnia PIP in the full table does not change that gate. The original LAVA family failed QC, no candidate met the project’s positive evidence-class gates, and none has compatible independent two-trait locus replication.','', '## Provenance and checks','', 'The mirror is pinned at revision `04820dafc5af625d1d941e080b5ae7d2b17dae87`; its claimed original source checksum and input/output hashes are recorded in `avi_provenance.json`. Its README describes a long table, but the delivered Parquet uses three score columns per position. The assumed alphabetical alternative-allele order was spot-checked against published original-file examples for reference A and T and against Broad SpliceAI Lookup for all three alternatives at one C-reference and one G-reference site. An independent Broad lookup also returned PHRED 20.00 for rs2431108, consistent with the mirror’s 19.99941 after rounding. These spot checks do not prove every mirror record; the original 88.5 GB file was not independently hashed.','', 'AlphaGenome and AVI are research tools, not clinical decision tools. The static AVI download and the API have different terms; see `mirror_LICENSE.txt` and the [AlphaGenome output terms](https://deepmind.google.com/science/alphagenome/output-terms). This pilot does not train a variant-effect model. Review the separate tissue-specific predictions against independent functional evidence; further Atlas track scoring can use an API key.','', 'Sources: [AlphaGenome Atlas research report](https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.09.16.26363192v1.full), [AlphaGenome model paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-10014-0), [pinned AVI mirror](https://huggingface.co/datasets/just-dna-seq/alphagenome_avi/tree/04820dafc5af625d1d941e080b5ae7d2b17dae87), [Broad score lookup](https://github.com/broadinstitute/SpliceAI-lookup/tree/main/google_cloud_run_services/score_lookup).','']
(Q/'AVI_PILOT_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
print('Wrote AVI pilot report')
